  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "They had crossed a continent on foot, and the last of them came over the pass at dawn.",
      "shot": 0,
      "at": 0.25,
      "seconds": 4.96
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Every man there went down on his knees when he saw the valley.",
      "shot": 1,
      "at": 5.75,
      "seconds": 4.28
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Their leader told them it was the promised land, and that it was theirs.",
      "shot": 2,
      "at": 10.542,
      "seconds": 4.42
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Among them was John Ferrier, who had walked out of the desert carrying a child.",
      "shot": 3,
      "at": 15.875,
      "seconds": 4.99
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "In three years he was comfortable, in nine he was rich, in twelve he had no equal.",
      "shot": 4,
      "at": 21.375,
      "seconds": 5.88
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The child grew up in the log house and worked beside him at everything.",
      "shot": 5,
      "at": 27.792,
      "seconds": 4.46
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The mountain air and the pines did for her what a mother would have done.",
      "shot": 6,
      "at": 32.792,
      "seconds": 3.84
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "So the bud opened into a flower, in the year her father became the richest of them.",
      "shot": 7,
      "at": 37.458,
      "seconds": 5.28
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "It was a warm June morning, and the whole valley was at work.",
      "shot": 8,
      "at": 43.25,
      "seconds": 4.06
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The gold fever had broken out west, and the road to it ran through the city.",
      "shot": 9,
      "at": 47.833,
      "seconds": 4.0
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Through the middle of it all Lucy Ferrier came galloping in on her father's errand.",
      "shot": 10,
      "at": 52.333,
      "seconds": 5.49
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "She was nineteen, and she had ridden that road a hundred times alone.",
      "shot": 11,
      "at": 58.333,
      "seconds": 5.68
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Strangers turned in the dust to watch her go by.",
      "shot": 12,
      "at": 64.542,
      "seconds": 3.49
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "At the edge of the city the road was stopped by a drove of cattle.",
      "shot": 13,
      "at": 68.833,
      "seconds": 4.19
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "She saw a gap and put her horse into it, and the beasts closed up behind her.",
      "shot": 14,
      "at": 73.542,
      "seconds": 5.14
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A horn came round and struck the mustang in the flank.",
      "shot": 15,
      "at": 79.208,
      "seconds": 3.69
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "It went up, and a slip would have put her under four hundred hooves.",
      "shot": 16,
      "at": 83.417,
      "seconds": 3.7
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "You're not hurt, I hope, miss.",
      "shot": 17,
      "at": 87.625,
      "seconds": 2.58
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "I guess you are the daughter of John Ferrier.",
      "shot": 18,
      "at": 90.708,
      "seconds": 3.0
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "lucy_ferrier",
      "text": "Hadn't you better come and ask him yourself?",
      "shot": 19,
      "at": 94.208,
      "seconds": 2.63
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "She rode on. He sat his horse in the road and watched the dust take her.",
      "shot": 20,
      "at": 97.375,
      "seconds": 4.8
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He came to the house that night, and a great many nights after it.",
      "shot": 21,
      "at": 103.083,
      "seconds": 4.94
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He had been a scout, a trapper and a miner, and he could tell it.",
      "shot": 22,
      "at": 108.542,
      "seconds": 3.72
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Her father heard him gladly. Lucy said very little at all.",
      "shot": 23,
      "at": 112.792,
      "seconds": 4.36
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "What she felt was plain enough to the one man it was meant for.",
      "shot": 24,
      "at": 117.667,
      "seconds": 4.7
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "By midsummer her heart was no longer her own, and she knew it.",
      "shot": 25,
      "at": 122.875,
      "seconds": 4.0
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He came down the road one evening at a gallop and pulled up at the gate.",
      "shot": 26,
      "at": 127.792,
      "seconds": 3.92
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "I am off, Lucy. Will you be ready to come when I am here again?",
      "shot": 27,
      "at": 132.25,
      "seconds": 4.14
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "lucy_ferrier",
      "text": "And when will that be?",
      "shot": 28,
      "at": 136.917,
      "seconds": 2.05
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "In two months you shall see me.",
      "shot": 29,
      "at": 140.667,
      "seconds": 2.5
    }
  ]
}